WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.872
JENNY BROWN: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.872 --> 00:00:04.410
about the new E2 VMs,
Packet Mirroring,

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.090
and climate data sets.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.970
I'm Jenny Brown, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.700
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.540
Google Compute Engine is a
powerful tool for any cloud

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.220
solution you want to build.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.230
And we want to make
sure great solutions are

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.270
available to everyone.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.900
To help with that, we've begun
the beta program for the new E2

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.400
Virtual Machines.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.190
These general purpose
VMs are cost optimized

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.360
without compromising
flexibility or reliability.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.940
And speaking of
beta programs, we've

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.850
also just launched
Packet Mirroring to beta.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.830
Packet Mirroring allows
you to troubleshoot

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:45.120
your existing virtual private
clouds using third party tools,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.690
ensure the security and
compliance of your workloads

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.840
by identifying network
anomalies at all levels--

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.430
across VPCs, between VMs, and
even down the line to your end

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.280
locations.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.830
Google Public Datasets
or a collection of data

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:03.830
sets that are available
at no charge to anyone

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.500
wanting to explore
modern data analytics

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.250
or researching innovative
solutions to complex problems.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.500
We're excited to be a
part of this collaboration

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.610
to host the latest climate
simulation data in the cloud.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.680
Now researchers all
around the globe

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.310
can use updated and consistent
environmental data models

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.680
without downloading
terabytes of data.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.990
The "Art of SLOs"
is a workshop that

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:31.140
teaches the essential elements
of developing service level

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:35.250
objectives to audiences
from Dev, Ops, product,

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.690
and business.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.060
And now we're releasing
the workshop materials

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.350
under a Creative
Commons license.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.920
So anyone may host their
own version of this workshop

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.160
to teach their coworkers
or customers, best friends,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.600
you name it.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.760
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.430
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.050
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.180
Go ahead and leave us
a comment or tweet us.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.420
We'll see it in the cloud.

